<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The adrenaline shot's effect, MDWC_Adrenaline since a DefOf field is named by its def and
    the ability already holds MDWC_AdrenalineShot (Ability_AdrenalineShot applies it; design in
    Docs/Specs/Adrenaline-Shot.md 3.2): go-juice's high (Core, Drugs/GoJuice.xml) on a short
    clock, with no tolerance and no addiction, pure XML. Hediff_High is go-juice's class and only
    shows the severity as a percentage. The shot sets severity 1, and severityPerDay -4 fades it
    in six hours. Severity falls at a constant rate, so each stage's band is its share of the
    clock: the rush and steady a sixteenth each (22.5 minutes), wearing off an eighth (45
    minutes), and the crash below wearing off's minSeverity 0.75 the last three quarters (four
    and a half hours). The comp steps every 200 ticks, about 0.013 of severity at this rate, and
    no threshold sits on a step, so no stage boundary hangs on a float comparison. The boost (the
    three levels above the crash, an hour and a half) and the crash (four and a half hours) are
    two mod settings written onto
    severityPerDay and the stages' minSeverity: the crash's band is its share of the total, and
    the boost keeps the split above, a quarter, a quarter and a half, at any length. A shot
    already given keeps the rate it was applied with, since vanilla's comp caches it per
    instance, while the thresholds are read live, so its levels move to a new split. A second shot
    refreshes the severity rather than adding to it, so a patient is never above 1, and a
    crashing patient can be shot straight back to the rush.

    Stages are listed ascending by minSeverity as vanilla requires, so the top level is last.
    The rush is go-juice's pain, Consciousness and Moving without its Sight; the next two taper
    those by thirds, and no level touches Sight. The boost is a burst of an hour and a half, spent on
    the fight it was given for. The crash is the cost the player feels, since rest is paid
    invisibly: no pain relief, Consciousness -0.10 and Moving -0.20 for four and a half hours, a patient
    dulled and slowed through the afternoon after the fight. Moving is kept at -0.20 because
    Consciousness feeds Moving, so the two stack. The comedown is each stage's restFallFactor,
    vanilla's own lever: none in the rush, then 1.25, 1.5 and 3 in the crash, so the bill rises
    as the boost thins and almost all of it lands in the crash. A full shot costs about 0.38 of
    rest beyond the 0.24 six waking hours cost anyway (9.5 extra waking hours' worth, at
    0.04 an hour), paid continuously while awake and not at all asleep; a longer crash setting
    raises the bill with it. The factors have no setting. The pilot's own RestFallRateFactor
    multiplies on top.

    everCurableByItem false: a healer mech serum must not spend itself on a stimulant. No
    scenarioCanAdd: it is the shoulders' to give. Under Combat Extended the boost levels also
    carry go-juice's suppression resistance and the crash a suppression penalty
    (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/AdrenalineSuppression.xml, by stage label).
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>MDWC_Adrenaline</defName>
    <hediffClass>Hediff_High</hediffClass>
    <label>adrenaline</label>
    <labelNoun>an adrenaline shot</labelNoun>
    <description>Adrenaline in the bloodstream. It dulls pain and quickens movement and thought, then gives way to a long crash. The body tires faster and faster as it wears off.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(1,0,0.5)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-4</severityPerDay>
        <showHoursToRecover>true</showHoursToRecover>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>crash</label>
        <restFallFactor>3</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.20</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>wearing off</label>
        <minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.7</painFactor>
        <restFallFactor>1.5</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.07</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.17</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>steady</label>
        <minSeverity>0.875</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.4</painFactor>
        <restFallFactor>1.25</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.13</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.33</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>rush</label>
        <minSeverity>0.9375</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.1</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.20</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.50</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>
</Defs>
